WEBVTT

00:00:15.555 --> 00:00:17.155
Whoa! What the...

00:00:17.595 --> 00:00:18.635
(GASPS, LAUGHS)

00:00:19.755 --> 00:00:20.755
(GRUNTS)

00:00:20.835 --> 00:00:21.875
(LAUGHS)

00:00:21.995 --> 00:00:23.635
(WHOOPS, LAUGHS)

00:00:24.555 --> 00:00:26.235
(OLAF GRUNTS, LAUGHS)

00:00:36.355 --> 00:00:37.795
ANNA: Whoa.

00:00:44.955 --> 00:00:47.635
Promise me,
we do this together, okay?

00:00:47.795 --> 00:00:49.155
I promise.

00:00:58.435 --> 00:00:59.955
-(SVEN GROANS)
-It's okay.

00:01:00.155 --> 00:01:02.275
Did you know
that an enchanted forest

00:01:02.355 --> 00:01:03.955
is a place of transformation?

00:01:04.115 --> 00:01:05.875
I have no idea
what that means...

00:01:06.035 --> 00:01:07.795
but I can't wait to see

00:01:07.875 --> 00:01:11.195
what it's gonna do
to each one of us.

00:01:11.595 --> 00:01:12.635
(WHOOSHING)

00:01:12.755 --> 00:01:14.075
ELSA: Hey!
KRISTOFF: What is this?

00:01:14.235 --> 00:01:15.515
ANNA: No pushing.
KRISTOFF: Stop it.

00:01:15.635 --> 00:01:16.835
-Whoa, whoa, whoa!
-ELSA: It's too fast.

00:01:17.475 --> 00:01:18.715
What was that?

00:01:18.795 --> 00:01:20.355
(OLAF LAUGHING)

00:01:20.715 --> 00:01:22.035
ANNA: No. No, no, no.

00:01:22.355 --> 00:01:23.595
(BOTH GASP)

00:01:24.275 --> 00:01:25.955
ANNA: And we're locked in.

00:01:26.035 --> 00:01:27.555
Probably should have seen
that one coming.

00:01:27.955 --> 00:01:29.235
(OLAF LAUGHING)

00:01:29.795 --> 00:01:32.195
This forest is beautiful.

00:01:32.955 --> 00:01:33.955
OLAF: Ooh.

00:01:34.395 --> 00:01:36.395
(CHITTERING AND TWITTERING
IN DISTANCE)

00:01:47.555 --> 00:01:48.675
(MOANS)

00:01:58.035 --> 00:02:01.555
The dam. It still stands.

00:02:01.755 --> 00:02:04.355
It was
in Grand Pabbie's visions.

00:02:04.555 --> 00:02:05.875
But why?

00:02:06.035 --> 00:02:08.795
I don't know, but it's still
in good shape. Thank goodness.

00:02:08.955 --> 00:02:09.995
What do you mean?

00:02:10.075 --> 00:02:11.155
Well, if that dam broke...

00:02:11.315 --> 00:02:13.315
it would send
a tidal wave so big

00:02:13.395 --> 00:02:15.675
it would wash away everything
on this fjord.

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.275
Everything?

00:02:17.355 --> 00:02:19.155
But Arendelle's on this fjord.

00:02:19.755 --> 00:02:21.835
Nothing's gonna happen
to Arendelle, Anna.

00:02:21.915 --> 00:02:23.155
It's gonna be fine.

00:02:23.315 --> 00:02:25.075
-Come here.
-(SIGHS)

00:02:25.155 --> 00:02:26.675
(SVEN SNORTS)

00:02:27.155 --> 00:02:28.955
(SNORTING)

00:02:29.035 --> 00:02:30.035
(GASPS SOFTLY)

00:02:30.115 --> 00:02:33.395
(CLEARS THROAT) You know,
under different circumstances,

00:02:33.475 --> 00:02:36.755
this would be a, uh,
pretty romantic place.

00:02:36.835 --> 00:02:37.835
Don't you think?

00:02:37.915 --> 00:02:38.915
Different circumstances?

00:02:38.995 --> 00:02:40.155
You mean,
like with someone else?

00:02:40.235 --> 00:02:41.955
What? No! No.

00:02:42.035 --> 00:02:43.395
I'm saying... (CLEARS THROAT)

00:02:43.475 --> 00:02:44.675
Just in case we don't make it
out of here...

00:02:44.755 --> 00:02:45.755
Wait, what?

00:02:45.835 --> 00:02:47.155
You don't think we're gonna
make it out of here?

00:02:47.235 --> 00:02:48.235
No. No!

00:02:48.315 --> 00:02:50.115
I mean, no,
we will make it out of here.

00:02:50.275 --> 00:02:51.635
Well, technically the odds are
kind of complicated,

00:02:51.715 --> 00:02:52.715
-but my point is...
-(GROANS)

00:02:53.195 --> 00:02:54.435
In case we die...

00:02:54.595 --> 00:02:56.915
-You think we're gonna die?
-No! No, no, no.

00:02:56.995 --> 00:02:58.195
-Where's Elsa?
-We will die at some point.

00:02:58.275 --> 00:02:59.435
ANNA: I swore that
I wouldn't leave her side.

00:02:59.515 --> 00:03:00.675
KRISTOFF: Not in any
recent time will we die.

00:03:00.755 --> 00:03:02.115
-ANNA: Elsa!
-But way far in the future,

00:03:02.195 --> 00:03:03.475
we will die.

00:03:03.555 --> 00:03:04.635
(GRUNTS)

00:03:06.275 --> 00:03:07.355
(SVEN MOANS)

00:03:07.435 --> 00:03:09.515
-Don't patronize me.
-(SVEN SNORTS)

00:03:11.715 --> 00:03:13.555
(CHITTERING)

00:03:14.515 --> 00:03:15.955
(RUSTLING)

00:03:18.275 --> 00:03:19.475
Elsa!

00:03:19.635 --> 00:03:20.915
There you are.

00:03:21.075 --> 00:03:22.995
-You okay?
-I'm fine.

00:03:23.155 --> 00:03:24.755
Okay, good.

00:03:25.275 --> 00:03:26.915
Where's Olaf?

00:03:27.195 --> 00:03:28.315
Um...

00:03:28.435 --> 00:03:29.515
Anna?

00:03:29.955 --> 00:03:31.235
Elsa?

00:03:31.395 --> 00:03:32.835
Sven?

00:03:33.395 --> 00:03:34.995
Samantha?

00:03:35.595 --> 00:03:37.395
(WHEEZING LAUGH)

00:03:37.475 --> 00:03:40.435
I don't even know a Samantha.

00:03:40.515 --> 00:03:41.955
(LAUGHING HYSTERICALLY)

00:03:42.035 --> 00:03:43.435
(WIND WHISTLING)

00:03:43.515 --> 00:03:44.595
Whoa!

00:03:47.195 --> 00:03:48.195
Mm.

00:03:49.155 --> 00:03:50.315
(CHITTERING)

00:03:51.155 --> 00:03:52.555
That's normal.

00:03:53.795 --> 00:03:54.835
(GRUNTS)

00:03:58.915 --> 00:04:00.475
-(CHITTERING)
-(GASPS)

00:04:04.995 --> 00:04:06.915
-(CHITTERING)
-What was that?

00:04:07.075 --> 00:04:08.075
(GASPS)

00:04:08.155 --> 00:04:09.155
Samantha?

00:04:10.435 --> 00:04:12.195
(WHIMSICAL MUSIC PLAYING)

00:04:14.355 --> 00:04:17.555
(SINGING) This will all
make sense when I am older

00:04:18.555 --> 00:04:21.715
Someday I will see
that this makes sense

00:04:22.555 --> 00:04:26.195
One day when I'm old and wise
I'll think back and realize

00:04:26.355 --> 00:04:29.475
That these were all
completely normal events!

00:04:29.795 --> 00:04:30.995
(YELPS)

00:04:32.395 --> 00:04:35.995
I'll have all the answers
when I'm older

00:04:36.155 --> 00:04:40.315
Like why we're in this
dark enchanted wood

00:04:40.475 --> 00:04:42.555
I know in a couple years

00:04:42.675 --> 00:04:44.595
These will seem
like childish fears

00:04:44.675 --> 00:04:47.395
And so I know this isn't bad,
it's good

00:04:47.555 --> 00:04:48.835
Excuse me

00:04:49.795 --> 00:04:53.475
Growing up means adapting

00:04:53.835 --> 00:04:57.315
Puzzling out your world
and your place

00:04:57.515 --> 00:05:01.755
When I'm more mature
I'll feel totally secure

00:05:01.915 --> 00:05:05.875
Being watched by something
with a creepy, creepy face

00:05:05.955 --> 00:05:07.195
(WATER BUBBLING)

00:05:07.275 --> 00:05:08.995
(SCREAMING)

00:05:14.475 --> 00:05:15.515
(EAGLE SCREAMS)

00:05:16.595 --> 00:05:20.555
See, that will all make sense
when I am older

00:05:21.155 --> 00:05:24.155
So there's no need
to be terrified or tense

00:05:25.795 --> 00:05:28.715
I'll just dream about a time

00:05:28.875 --> 00:05:32.555
When I'm in my agèd prime

00:05:32.715 --> 00:05:35.075
'Cause when you're older

00:05:35.235 --> 00:05:40.435
Absolutely everything
makes sense!

00:05:40.595 --> 00:05:41.795
This is fine.

00:05:43.795 --> 00:05:45.675
-OLAF: Whoa!
-Olaf!

00:05:45.755 --> 00:05:47.355
(OLAF CACKLING)

00:05:47.435 --> 00:05:48.795
(ALL YELP)

00:05:50.435 --> 00:05:51.515
Hey, guys.

00:05:51.675 --> 00:05:53.475
Meet the Wind Spirit.

00:05:53.555 --> 00:05:55.235
(ALL YELPING)

00:05:55.315 --> 00:05:56.555
KRISTOFF: Coming through!

00:05:57.195 --> 00:05:58.475
Ooh, I think
I'm gonna be sick.

00:05:58.555 --> 00:06:01.355
I'd hold your hair back,
but I can't find my arms.

00:06:01.555 --> 00:06:03.355
-(SVEN BELLOWS)
-(YELPING)

00:06:05.395 --> 00:06:06.395
(GASPS)

00:06:08.435 --> 00:06:09.435
(GASPS)

00:06:09.555 --> 00:06:10.995
-(CHITTERING)
-Hey! Stop!

00:06:11.355 --> 00:06:12.995
(ALL WHIMPERING)

00:06:13.075 --> 00:06:14.915
-(KRISTOFF SCREAMING)
-(OLAF LAUGHING)

00:06:20.755 --> 00:06:21.915
(OLAF GRUNTS)

00:06:23.315 --> 00:06:24.315
Elsa!

00:06:24.755 --> 00:06:25.915
(GRUNTING)

00:06:27.475 --> 00:06:29.155
ANNA: Let her go!

00:06:31.875 --> 00:06:33.155
(STRAINING)

00:06:33.395 --> 00:06:34.875
KRISTOFF: Anna, be careful!

00:06:35.555 --> 00:06:37.155
That's my sister!

00:06:37.675 --> 00:06:39.115
(LAUGHTER)

00:06:41.515 --> 00:06:42.915
MATTIAS: Prince Agnarr!

00:06:43.635 --> 00:06:46.075
-(WEAPONS CLANGING)
-(GRUNTS)

00:06:46.675 --> 00:06:47.995
For Arendelle.

00:06:48.075 --> 00:06:49.315
(SWORD SWISHES)

00:06:50.795 --> 00:06:51.875
FIGHTER: Look out!

00:06:51.955 --> 00:06:53.235
(RUNEARD SCREAMS)

00:06:53.315 --> 00:06:54.675
-YOUNG AGNARR: Father!
-(ELSA GRUNTS)

00:07:00.115 --> 00:07:01.315
(BOTH PANT)

00:07:02.355 --> 00:07:03.715
(PANTING)

00:07:03.795 --> 00:07:05.795
-Are you okay?
-I'm fine.

00:07:06.195 --> 00:07:07.235
(SVEN SNIFFS)

00:07:07.315 --> 00:07:09.235
-What are these?
-(SVEN MOANS)

00:07:09.795 --> 00:07:12.955
Oh, they look like
moments in time.

00:07:13.835 --> 00:07:15.515
What's that thing
you say, Olaf?

00:07:15.675 --> 00:07:17.195
The thing... Oh!

00:07:17.275 --> 00:07:19.195
My theory
about advancing technologies

00:07:19.275 --> 00:07:20.675
as both our savior
and our doom?

00:07:20.755 --> 00:07:23.035
(STAMMERS) No, not that one.
The one about...

00:07:23.115 --> 00:07:24.315
-The one about cucumbers?
-No.

00:07:24.395 --> 00:07:25.395
The thing about water.

00:07:25.475 --> 00:07:27.835
Oh! Yeah.
Water has memory.

00:07:27.995 --> 00:07:29.635
The water
that makes up you and me

00:07:29.755 --> 00:07:31.715
has passed through
at least four humans...

00:07:31.795 --> 00:07:33.715
and/or animals before us.

00:07:34.635 --> 00:07:35.635
ANNA: Hmm.

00:07:35.995 --> 00:07:38.435
And remembers everything.

00:07:38.515 --> 00:07:39.555
(SVEN GRUNTING)

00:07:39.635 --> 00:07:41.675
(CHUCKLES) The wind's back.

00:07:41.755 --> 00:07:43.875
(EXCLAIMS) Delicious.

00:07:44.035 --> 00:07:46.795
I think I'll name you Gale.

00:07:47.435 --> 00:07:48.635
(EXCLAIMS)

00:07:48.715 --> 00:07:50.355
-Get out of there. Whoa!
-(CHITTERING)

00:07:50.995 --> 00:07:52.835
-Oh. Hi.
-Aren't you curious?

00:07:53.195 --> 00:07:54.595
-(GRUNTS)
-(ELSA CHUCKLES)

00:07:54.875 --> 00:07:56.835
-You in a better mood now?
-(ANNA GIGGLES)

00:08:01.315 --> 00:08:02.355
(ANNA GASPS)

00:08:06.995 --> 00:08:10.195
Father. That's Father.

00:08:12.115 --> 00:08:13.435
This girl.

00:08:13.635 --> 00:08:15.235
OLAF: She's saving him.

00:08:15.795 --> 00:08:17.195
She's Northuldra.

00:08:17.275 --> 00:08:19.475
-(HIGH-PITCHED CHITTERING)
-(ALL GASP)

00:08:19.595 --> 00:08:20.875
What is that?

00:08:21.035 --> 00:08:22.795
-ELSA: Olaf, get behind me.
-(WHIMPERS)

00:08:25.475 --> 00:08:26.595
What are you gonna do
with that?

00:08:26.755 --> 00:08:27.835
I have no idea.

00:08:28.115 --> 00:08:29.915
(CHITTERING CONTINUES)

